# Cargo test gate

When verifying Rust changes (compiler, VM, parser, CLI, or CI), **do not** run bare `cargo test` or package-only suites as the sole check.

## Required local / agent commands

```bash
cargo test --workspace --all-targets
```

Retry once on transient macOS/EAGAIN listing failures (same as CI).

`--all-targets` is required: integration tests under `*/tests/` (e.g. `compiler/tests/diagnostics.rs`, `perf_metrics.rs`) and bins/examples are **not** covered by lib-only or default-member `cargo test`.

## Feature-gated suites

Optional crate features must be exercised when touching gated code or when catching CI-shaped failures:

| Feature | Typical flag | Notes |
|---------|--------------|--------|
| default stack | _(none)_ | `crypto` + `time` + `regex` + `tls` |
| `crypto` / `time` / `regex` / `tls` | `--no-default-features --features <name>` | isolate which optional dep broke |
| `dissect` | `--features dissect` | compiler dissect + its integration tests |
| `debugger` | `--features debugger` | machine debugger paths |

Example isolation run:

```bash
cargo test --workspace --all-targets --no-default-features --features tls
cargo test --workspace --all-targets --features dissect
```

## Related gates

- Lint: `cargo check --workspace` (not clippy — `Gc::payload_mut` deny).
- Language harness (after a debug `coil` build): `./target/debug/coil test`.
